   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-decision-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 1221.0,
   "width": 1394,
   "height": 157.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 356696218,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1371822052,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "We choose A. Development gate: run our workflow on Bruckner's 2025-11-10 snapshot and compare with the reviewers' final labels, per trial and per part (participants, outcomes,\ncancelled), until every disagreement is explained as our bug (fixed), data that changed after their review (set aside) or a likely labelling error (noted). Extended deadlines come from\nBruckner's flag, because they used non-public data.\n\nEach verdict carries a verdict confidence from 0 to 100%: our model's internal certainty about that one trial's verdict. At 99% or above it may be published; below 99% it needs manual\napproval. The 99% line is set during this development: verdicts we score at 99% or above must match the reviewers at least 99% of the time. Every verdict stores its decision record:\nverdict; confidence; per-part results with quote and page; threshold and config version; model id and prompt version; a short reason.",
   "originalText": "We choose A. Development gate: run our workflow on Bruckner's 2025-11-10 snapshot and compare with the reviewers' final labels, per trial and per part (participants, outcomes, cancelled), until every disagreement is explained as our bug (fixed), data that changed after their review (set aside) or a likely labelling error (noted). Extended deadlines come from Bruckner's flag, because they used non-public data.\n\nEach verdict carries a verdict confidence from 0 to 100%: our model's internal certainty about that one trial's verdict. At 99% or above it may be published; below 99% it needs manual approval. The 99% line is set during this development: verdicts we score at 99% or above must match the reviewers at least 99% of the time. Every verdict stores its decision record: verdict; confidence; per-part results with quote and page; threshold and config version; model id and prompt version; a short reason.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-decision",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "t11",
   "type": "text",
